lius Caesar was kidnapped by pirates, and demanded they raise his ransom?", "s": 0.05, "e": 6.692}, {"text": "In 75 BC, Cilician pirates captured 25-year-old Caesar in the Aegean Sea and asked for 20 talents of silver.", "s": 6.872, "e": 16.949}, {"text": "Offended, Caesar laughed and told them he was worth at least 50.", "s": 17.069, "e": 21.22}, {"text": "While waiting 38 days for the money, he bossed the pirates around, ordered them to be quiet while he slept, and joked that he would return and crucify them all.", "s": 21.34, "e": 32.276}, {"text": "Once released, he raised a fleet, hunted them down, and kept his promise.", "s": 32.396, "e": 37.127}]}